The development of the neuron doctrine was marked by a fierce debate between two scientists: Camillo Golgi and Santiago Ramón y Cajal. The debate, known as the ""Reticular theory vs. Retinetic theory,"" was a major turning point in the study of the nervous system. The debate was later resolved in favor of Cajal's retinitic theory, which is the neuron doctrine.
