\[ \phi_1^T M \phi_2 = m_t \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \end{bmatrix} \begin{bmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{bmatrix} = m_t (1 - 1 + 0) = 0 \]  

Similarly, \( \phi_1^T M \phi_3 = 0 \) and \( \phi_2^T M \phi_3 = 0 \).  

**Final Answer:**  
The natural frequencies are:  
1. \( \omega_1 = \boxed{6,140 \, \text{rad/s}} \)  
2. \( \omega_2 = \boxed{7,150 \, \text{rad/s}} \)  
3. \( \omega_3 = \boxed{7,150 \, \text{rad/s}} \)  

